- Both refs are correctly typed
- Type check passes

## Issue
The `onCreateProject` callback in `TextureEditorWrapper.tsx` has no error handling. If project creation fails, the error is unhandled.

## File
`src/components/texture-editor/TextureEditorWrapper.tsx` (lines 91-95)

## Current Code
```tsx
onCreateProject={async (name) => {
  const newId = await createNewProject(name);
  const currentPath = mode === "full" ? "/texture-editor" : "/";
  window.location.href = `${currentPath}?project-id=${newId}`;
}}
```

## Problem
- If `createNewProject(name)` throws, the promise rejection is unhandled
- User sees no feedback on failure
- Compare to `CommonToolbar.tsx` which has proper try/catch with error logging

## Fix
```tsx
onCreateProject={async (name) => {
  try {
    const newId = await createNewProject(name);
    const currentPath = mode === "full" ? "/texture-editor" : "/";
    window.location.href = `${currentPath}?project-id=${newId}`;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("[TextureEditorWrapper] Failed to create project:", error);
    // Error is shown by ProjectSelectionModal via its catch block
  }
}}
```

## Note
The `ProjectSelectionModal` already has a catch block that sets an error message, so this try/catch is mainly for logging. However, the current code will cause an unhandled promise rejection.

