## Objective
Add the useFrame hook that applies the animation each frame.

## File to Modify
`/src/hooks/useModelAnimation.ts`

## Code to Add After useEffect
```typescript
  // Animation frame - check for progress changes and apply animation
  useFrame(() => {
    // Check if progress changed and update spring
    const targetProgress = getProgress();
    if (targetProgress \!== lastProgressRef.current) {
      lastProgressRef.current = targetProgress;
      progress.start(targetProgress);
    }

    // Early return if clip or group not ready
    const clip = clipRef.current;
    if (\!clip || \!groupRef.current) return;

    // Get current spring-interpolated progress value
    const currentProgress = progress.get();

    // Convert progress (0-1) to animation time
    const animTime = clip.duration * currentProgress;

    // Apply animation to all tracks in the clip
    for (const track of clip.tracks) {
      // Parse track name: "objectName.propertyName" (e.g., "lid.position")
      const [objectName, propertyName] = track.name.split('.');

      // Find the target object in the scene graph
      const targetObject = groupRef.current.getObjectByName(objectName);
      if (\!targetObject) continue;

      // Sample the track at current time
      const sampledValues = sampleTrackAtTime(track, animTime);

      // Apply sampled values based on property type
      if (propertyName === 'position') {
        targetObject.position.set(
          sampledValues[0],
          sampledValues[1],
          sampledValues[2],
        );
      } else if (propertyName === 'quaternion') {
        targetObject.quaternion.set(
          sampledValues[0],
          sampledValues[1],
          sampledValues[2],
          sampledValues[3],
        );
      } else if (propertyName === 'scale') {
        targetObject.scale.set(
          sampledValues[0],
          sampledValues[1],
          sampledValues[2],
        );
      }
    }
  });
```

## Key Implementation Details

### Progress Change Detection
- `getProgress()` reads directly from store (e.g., `useModelStore.getState().bogieTarget`)
- Avoids React re-renders by not using React state
- Only triggers spring.start() when value actually changes

### Track Name Format
- GLTF exports tracks as "objectName.propertyName"
- Example: "lid.quaternion", "wheel_back_left.position"
- We parse this to find the right object and apply the right transform

### Supported Property Types
- `position`: Vector3 (3 values)
- `quaternion`: Quaternion (4 values)
- `scale`: Vector3 (3 values)

